{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-nzxd-n5zv-wdnw-3t7s","published":"2026-11-20T18:08:38Z","modified":"2026-11-24T11:45:02.741258752Z","upstream":["CVE-2025-6297"],"summary":"It was discovered that dpkg-deb does not properly sanitize directory permissions when extracting a control member into…","details":"It was discovered that dpkg-deb does not properly sanitize directory permissions when extracting a control member into a temporary directory, which is\ndocumented as being a safe operation even on untrusted data. This may result in leaving temporary files behind on cleanup. Given automated and repeated execution of dpkg-deb commands on\nadversarial .deb packages or with well compressible files, placed\ninside a directory with permissions not allowing removal by a non-root\nuser, this can end up in a DoS scenario due to causing disk quota\nexhaustion or disk full conditions.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"dpkg","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.23","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/dpkg"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"1.22.21-r0"}]}],"versions":["1.22.21-r0","1.22.21-r1"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-nzxd-n5zv-wdnw-3t7s.json"}},{"package":{"name":"dpkg","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/dpkg"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"1.23.7-r0"}]}],"versions":["1.23.7-r0"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-nzxd-n5zv-wdnw-3t7s.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://scout.docker.com/v/DHI-nzxd-n5zv-wdnw-3t7s"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-6297"},{"type":"FIX","url":"https://git.dpkg.org/cgit/dpkg/dpkg.git/commit/?id=ed6bbd445dd8800308c67236ba35d08004c98e82"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2025-6297"},{"type":"